<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Titelberg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Titelberg is a plateau in south-western Luxembourg, near Differdange, that held one of the largest oppida of the Treveri, a fortified Celtic town of about 40 hectares occupied from the 2nd century BCE. Excavations have found a mint, workshops, a public assembly area and Roman imports. After the Roman conquest it continued as a smaller settlement before being overshadowed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trier">Trier</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/titelberg.jpg" alt="Titelberg" width="320" height="217" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TimeTravelRome · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Titelberg1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
